    "The tightly bunched probabilities among France, Spain, England, Portugal, Argentina, and Brazil reflect a deep pool of contenders entering the expanded 48-team tournament, where squad depth, recent Nations League and qualifying form, and favorable group-stage matchups have kept multiple sides within striking distance of lifting the trophy. Spain and France sit atop the implied probabilities due to their blend of young attacking talent and defensive organization, though concerns over key player availability continue to influence trader positioning. England\u2019s strong club representation and historical knockout pedigree sustain their mid-teens chance, while Portugal and the South American duo of defending champions Argentina and star-laden Brazil retain realistic paths through experience and individual quality. Lower-tier European and emerging sides trail as underdogs with limited recent evidence of challenging the elite."
